  "student_passage": "Our science club arranged a walk through the wetland near town. We wrote (1) ____ names on a list and met at the school gate. Everyone had (2) ____ a bottle of water and a small notebook. Our teacher arrived even (3) ____ than usual because she wanted to check the route before we set off.\n\nShe asked us to speak (4) ____ near the birds. Several signs explained the (5) ____ between the paths open to visitors and those kept closed for wildlife. I wanted to go straight to the lake, (6) ____ the teacher said the higher path would let us see more of the area first.\n\nWe walked (7) ____ a narrow wooden bridge. One side of it was wet, and I stepped into a shallow puddle. Both my (8) ____ were soon damp, but my spare socks were safely wrapped in my bag. The teacher had (9) ____ us to bring them during the previous lesson, and I was glad I had listened.\n\nThis was the (10) ____ visit I had made to the wetland. On the first visit, I had hurried past the signs. This time, I noticed how the different paths fitted together. We sat on a bench by the lake and drew the route before walking back to the bus stop.",
