  "filled_passage": "Our science club arranged a walk through the wetland near town. We wrote (1) our names on a list and met at the school gate. Everyone had (2) brought a bottle of water and a small notebook. Our teacher arrived even (3) earlier than usual because she wanted to check the route before we set off.\n\nShe asked us to speak (4) quietly near the birds. Several signs explained the (5) differences between the paths open to visitors and those kept closed for wildlife. I wanted to go straight to the lake, (6) but the teacher said the higher path would let us see more of the area first.\n\nWe walked (7) across a narrow wooden bridge. One side of it was wet, and I stepped into a shallow puddle. Both my (8) feet were soon damp, but my spare socks were safely wrapped in my bag. The teacher had (9) taught us to bring them during the previous lesson, and I was glad I had listened.\n\nThis was the (10) second visit I had made to the wetland. On the first visit, I had hurried past the signs. This time, I noticed how the different paths fitted together. We sat on a bench by the lake and drew the route before walking back to the bus stop.",
